    <string name="buttondebug_howto_title">A full check</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_1">Close any other game screens, then Reset stats.</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_2">Chase 1→4: the LEDs should light %1$s. If the order is off, fix the colour on each tile (or the wiring).</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_order_unknown">in id order</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_3">Tap each button 20 times: slow, then as fast as you can. Each tile should read 20, with accepted equal to reached games, and lost, noise and short counts at 0.</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_4">Hold each for 2 seconds, then let go. The count goes up by exactly one.</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_5">Switch the LEDs to Follow press and tap. The LED should light the instant the button goes down.</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_6">Wiggle each button\'s wires while it\'s untouched. Any edge in the log means a loose connection.</string>
    <string name="buttondebug_howto_7">Watch Bounce, release (max). If it gets near half the debounce setting, raise the debounce.</string>
